  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 13 files needed for this dependency-graph analysis.\n\n**Log4j2 side (bridge module restructuring):**\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml` + `SLF4JProvider.java` \u2014 the Log4j2-API\u2192SLF4J bridge (used when app code calls Log4j2 API but SLF4J/Logback is the backend), registered as a `Provider` (priority 15, `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory`).\n- `log4j-slf4j-impl/pom.xml` vs `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml` \u2014 the two SLF4J\u2192Log4j2-core bindings (SLF4J 1.x vs SLF4J 2.x `SLF4JServiceProvider`), the actual \"restructuring\" split introduced for SLF4J 2.0 support.\n- `log4j-api/spi/Provider.java` + `log4j-api/LogManager.java` \u2014 the SPI Log4j2 uses to discover/prioritize logging-context providers at runtime.\n- `log4j-api/pom.xml` \u2014 version anchor (2.20.0).\n\n**Spring Boot side (auto-configuration/detection):**\n- `spring-boot-starter-logging/build.gradle` \u2014 depends on `log4j-to-slf4j` (default: Logback backend, Log4j2-API calls bridged to SLF4J).\n- `spring-boot-starter-log4j2/build.gradle` \u2014 depends on `log4j-slf4j2-impl` (alternative: Log4j2-core backend, SLF4J calls bridged to Log4j2).\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`, `LogbackLoggingSystem.java`, `LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 the auto-config detection logic (`ClassUtils.isPresent` checks for `Log4jContextFactory`/`LoggerContext` on the classpath).\n- `spring.factories` \u2014 registers both `LoggingSystemFactory` implementations for classpath-based auto-detection.",
